From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:51:15 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: skip a scanned BSS on a band or channel the
 wiphy doesn't have

brcmf_inform_single_bss() picks the band from the channel number alone,
turns it into a frequency and hands cfg80211 the result of
ieee80211_get_channel() unchecked. For a channel the wiphy doesn't
carry that lookup returns NULL, and cfg80211 dereferences it.

The firmware does report such BSSes. A 6 GHz chanspec's channel number
is read as a 2.4 or 5 GHz one (6 GHz channel 37 becomes 5185 MHz,
which no band has), and since brcmf_construct_chaninfo() skips 6 GHz
chanspecs there is no 6 GHz band to find it in anyway. A 5 GHz channel
the band table doesn't have does the same: on a Pixel 9a (BCM4383)
every boot with Wi-Fi logs "brcmf_construct_chaninfo: Ignoring
unexpected firmware channel 177" (UNII-4). The boot that crashed had
just warned "Invalid chanspec 0x5001" (6 GHz, channel 1) from an older
brcmutil without the 6 GHz band; which BSS the scan was reporting when
it crashed wasn't logged. Once, from the escan timeout worker:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000000
  Workqueue: events brcmf_cfg80211_escan_timeout_worker [brcmfmac]
  pc : cfg80211_inform_single_bss_data+0xb0/0x4fc [cfg80211]
  Call trace:
   cfg80211_inform_single_bss_data+0xb0/0x4fc [cfg80211] (P)
   cfg80211_inform_bss_data+0xbc/0x12d4 [cfg80211]
   brcmf_inform_single_bss+0x190/0x20c [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_cfg80211_escan_timeout_worker+0x80/0xec [brcmfmac]

The worker died inside cfg80211's RCU read-side section, so the next
system suspend couldn't freeze khugepaged (stuck in lru_add_drain_all())
and the phone reset a few seconds later.

Decode the chanspec for every BSS and skip a 6 GHz one first, then keep
a NULL check on the channel as the backstop. A 6 GHz BSS whose channel
number also exists on 2.4 or 5 GHz (1, 5, 9, 149 and so on) was
reported until now on the wrong band; it now drops out of the scan list,
which is a visible change on any chip whose firmware reports 6 GHz. Both return 0 with a debug
message, so the rest of the scan list is still reported:
brcmf_inform_bss() stops at the first error.

Fixes: 5b435de0d786 ("net: wireless: add brcm80211 drivers")
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c    | 20 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 5c43cd380..84341e7f8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -3440,7 +3440,7 @@ static s32 brcmf_inform_single_bss(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 	struct brcmf_pub *drvr = cfg->pub;
 	struct cfg80211_bss *bss;
 	enum nl80211_band band;
-	struct brcmu_chan ch;
+	struct brcmu_chan ch = {};
 	u16 channel;
 	u32 freq;
 	u16 notify_capability;
@@ -3454,11 +3454,16 @@ static s32 brcmf_inform_single_bss(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (!bi->ctl_ch) {
-		ch.chspec = le16_to_cpu(bi->chanspec);
-		cfg->d11inf.decchspec(&ch);
-		bi->ctl_ch = ch.control_ch_num;
+	ch.chspec = le16_to_cpu(bi->chanspec);
+	cfg->d11inf.decchspec(&ch);
+	/* No 6 GHz band is registered (brcmf_construct_chaninfo() skips it) */
+	if (ch.band == BRCMU_CHAN_BAND_6G) {
+		brcmf_dbg(SCAN, "%pM: 6 GHz chanspec 0x%04x, skipped\n",
+			  bi->BSSID, ch.chspec);
+		return 0;
 	}
+	if (!bi->ctl_ch)
+		bi->ctl_ch = ch.control_ch_num;
 	channel = bi->ctl_ch;
 
 	if (channel <= CH_MAX_2G_CHANNEL)
@@ -3468,6 +3473,11 @@ static s32 brcmf_inform_single_bss(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 
 	freq = ieee80211_channel_to_frequency(channel, band);
 	bss_data.chan = ieee80211_get_channel(wiphy, freq);
+	if (!bss_data.chan) {
+		brcmf_dbg(SCAN, "%pM: channel %d (%u MHz) not in the wiphy, skipped\n",
+			  bi->BSSID, channel, freq);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	bss_data.boottime_ns = ktime_to_ns(ktime_get_boottime());
 
 	notify_capability = le16_to_cpu(bi->capability);
